BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:4d47d949-0009-4a88-a828-3de5b4315df9@nectar2026
DTSTAMP:20260615T233644Z
DTSTART;TZID=America/Vancouver:20260619T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/Vancouver:20260619T200000
SUMMARY:Feelgood
LOCATION:Sunset Stage
DESCRIPTION:Hi\, I’m Aaron aka ‘Feelgood’. I grew up in the Toronto a
 rea and am heavily influenced by the rave culture of the late 90's and ear
 ly 00's. I’ve also spent a decade organizing and promoting events under 
 the brand Release. I held multiple weekly residencies for years which help
 ed me develop the ability to ‘play to the crowd’ and curate sounds to 
 fit with the energy of the room.\n\nWith 20+ years of collecting music I h
 ave a deep repository of sounds that I use to create unique sets with char
 acter. I have a lean towards sound system culture focused themes with a do
 se of melody inspired by the late 90's /early 00's progressive sounds that
  ultimately attracted me to the scene.\n\nMy goal is to bring intentionali
 ty to my sets and curate for time\, place and atmosphere.\n\nInstagram: ht
 tps://www.instagram.com/deejayfeelgood\n\nProfile: https://thenectarfestiv
 al.com/products/feelgood
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:7cd2e075-68cb-4d44-a0ed-15b7a7cc0e43@nectar2026
DTSTAMP:20260615T233644Z
DTSTART;TZID=America/Vancouver:20260619T200000
DTEND;TZID=America/Vancouver:20260619T213000
SUMMARY:Bedtime Snack
LOCATION:Sunset Stage
DESCRIPTION:Jayden\, also known as bedtime snack\, is an Indigenous artist 
 from the Kwakwaka’wakw ~ Wuikinuxv ~  Tla’amin nations\, deeply roote
 d in the Northwest Coast of so-called “British Columbia”.\n\nWhether i
 t’s drum and bass at sunrise\, or dubstep at sundown\, Jayden’s capaci
 ty to capture a feeling and then share it with the dancefloor sets him apa
 rt from his contemporaries.\n\nBridging the gap between high energy beats 
 and moody\, emotional dance music have brought him to play festivals such 
 as Bass Coast\, Samsara\, Pachena Bay\, Paradise\, and more. Almost every 
 selection is heavily influenced or inspired by his first true loves - hip-
 hop and r&b.\n\nAcross live DJ sets and original productions\, bedtime sna
 ck’s emotive nature leans into a balance of creative expression\, reveal
 ing an undying love for the craft. If you’re eager to experience a thoug
 htfully curated set that lasts\, don’t go to bed without a bedtime snack
 .\n\nSoundCloud: https://soundcloud.com/bedtimesnack\nSpotify: https://ope
 n.spotify.com/artist/1JvPesW1isf5BqIZSCaCPK\nLinktree: http://linktr.ee/be
 dtimesnack\n\nProfile: https://thenectarfestival.com/products/bedtime-snac
 k
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:6ccb1cd0-effe-4ed5-bad3-4baf1fb62a9d@nectar2026
DTSTAMP:20260615T233644Z
DTSTART;TZID=America/Vancouver:20260620T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/Vancouver:20260620T213000
SUMMARY:Ephemeral Objects & IHA
LOCATION:Sunset Stage
DESCRIPTION:ephemeral objects moves between ethereal\, dubwise atmospheres\
 , textural grooves\, and ambient introspection\, with an affinity for deep
 \, hypnotic\, and experimental sounds. Her DJ sets are both meditative an
 d kinetic\, drawing from labels and producers operating at the fringes of 
 techno\, leftfield bass\, psychedelia\, and downtempo. Her productions ha
 ve been released on Wuji\, SYS Sister Sounds\, and Bass Coast Music.\n\nSh
 e is half of the a/v project i+eo with IHA\, which debuted their performan
 ce Portals at MUTEK Montreal 2025. She co-runs Acceleration Radio\, an a/v
  experimentation platform and FM radio program\, supporting emerging under
 ground talent from Vancouver and beyond.\n\nlinks:\n\nSoundCloud: https://
 soundcloud.com/ephemeral_objects\nInstagram: https://www.instagram.com/eph
 emeral.objects?igsh=MXZqNnBhaWhsamlrYw%3D%3D&utm_source=qr\nLinktree: http
 s://linktr.ee/ephemeralobjects\n\nProfile: https://thenectarfestival.com/p
 roducts/ephemeral-objects\n\n———\n\nHailing from the rich musical fa
 bric of Vancouver\, IHA is a producer\, DJ\, sound artist\, and curator be
 hind Naga\, a multimedia label and event platform. Rooted in memory\, drea
 ms\, and shifting perception\, their sets carry a curious\, instinctive en
 ergy—ranging from dubby atmospheres to playful techno and forward-thinki
 ng bass. Their debut EP “Diwa” released on Victoria label Pleasure Man
 agement this year\, with previous singles appearing on labels PPRZ\, Weird
 oes Inc\, Bass Coast Music\, Ommaya\, and Wuji.\n\nAs one-half of i+eo\, t
 hey have performed an audio visual set with ephemeral objects in Mutek Mon
 treal in 2025. Since 2021 they have played campouts and festivals both loc
 ally and across the pond: Bass Coast\, Future Forest\, Osmosis\, Ever Afte
 rs\, ADE\, and Honcho.\n\nLinktree: https://linktr.ee/agimat\nInstagram: h
 ttps://www.instagram.com/agimat.iha/\n\nProfile: https://thenectarfestival
 .com/products/iha
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:5106b8d9-abbb-4622-9b2d-5d51067f5de0@nectar2026
DTSTAMP:20260615T233644Z
DTSTART;TZID=America/Vancouver:20260621T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/Vancouver:20260621T190000
SUMMARY:Coco
LOCATION:Sunset Stage
DESCRIPTION:Coco is a multidisciplinary artist from Salt Spring Island with
  a gift for curating unforgettable vibes. A DJ\, tattoo artist\, drum make
 r\, hypnotherapist\, and women’s empowerment coach\, she brings depth\, 
 creativity\, and magnetic energy to everything she touches.\n\nShe plays a
  spectrum of music including rap\, femme rap\, R&B\, & dubstep to chill\, 
 melodic\, and deep sounds. This year at Nectar she will romanticize the de
 eper side of things—curating music to take listeners on a journey of sou
 lful connection.\n\nYou can catch Coco playing gigs around Salt Spring Isl
 and and the BC West Coast as another powerful form of creative expression.
 \n\nSoundCloud: https://on.soundcloud.com/Mt7t9WISAftxVPd5Rh\nInstagram: h
 ttps://www.instagram.com/natures.drum/\nInstagram: https://www.instagram.c
 om/corinnedonnellyhypnotherapy/\n\nProfile: https://thenectarfestival.com/
 products/coco
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:d2e412f6-0e9e-4d34-85d0-e2f31fbacd3d@nectar2026
DTSTAMP:20260615T233644Z
DTSTART;TZID=America/Vancouver:20260621T190000
DTEND;TZID=America/Vancouver:20260621T213000
SUMMARY:Ray Black & Michael Red
LOCATION:Sunset Stage
DESCRIPTION:Vancouver based artist Ray Black is an innovative DJ/Vocalist w
 ho’s work is transforming the face of electronic music. Ray takes inspir
 ation from artists within Future Beats\, Wave\, and Dub \; the result is a
 n ethereal yet hard-hitting sound uniquely his own. Listeners find themsel
 ves on a journey riding at the forefront of this ever growing musical move
 ment.\n\nCombining conscious lyrics and rhythmic beats\, his sound on its 
 own is a journey through space and time in a party atmosphere. With a natu
 ral and undeniable presence on the turntables\, Ray seamlessly incorporate
 s live vocals with original remixes and mashups. The overall aesthetic is 
 one that must not only be heard but witnessed to be fully experienced.\n\n
 Ray Black has been a DJ/ Vocalist  in Vancouver’s music scene for the p
 ast 10 years and during that time joined Hip Hop Collective Sweatshop Unio
 n.  Additionally\, Black’s diverse style has allowed him to tour around
  North America and play festivals including Shambhala\, Bass Coast\, SXSW\
 , Bamboo Bass Festival\, Astral Harvest and CMW\, where he has shared the 
 stage with artists such as Talib Kweli\, Mac Miller\, Craze\, Mr. Carmack 
 and Hilltop Hoods.\n\nCurrently in the studio working on new original mate
 rial. With a guided focus on creating something unique\, accessible and tr
 ansformative\, Black’s work will no doubt be a pioneering element in thi
 s thriving and ever changing bass music community.\n\nProfile: https://the
 nectarfestival.com/products/ray-black\n\n———\n\nMichael Red is a Va
 ncouver-based music producer\, film composer\, collaborator\, performer an
 d DJ with always a few handfuls of projects on the go. He is an active cur
 ator and event producer as well\, and works with local underground music/c
 reative community in a number of ways. Michael is recognized as playing 
 a critical role in shaping foundational sound system and underground elect
 ronic music culture in Western Canada\, as both an event creator and DJ. S
 ome of his projects include Low Indigo (events\, label\, community)\, Oro 
 Azul (with Ultima Esuna)\, a very active collaboration with Tsimka\, and L
 ight Blues (sound wellness based mixs\, releases and live sessions).\n\nLi
 nktree: https://linktr.ee/michaelred\nInstagram: https://www.instagram.com
 /michael__red\n\nProfile: https://thenectarfestival.com/products/michael-r
 ed
END:VEVENT
END:VCALENDAR
